itions on various contemporary news articles, medical drama series, and documentaries, students are encouraged to become Intercultural Communicative Citizens and learn the contents through the language. The expected student outcome is to gain confidence in the academic level of discussions and compositions by critical thinking and analyzing.", "catalogBreadth": "(GB)", "catalogDistr": "", "catalogEnrollmentPriority": null, "catalogLang": "Satisfies Option 1.", "catalogForbiddenOverlaps": "", "catalogAttribute": "", "catalogWhenOffered": "Fall.", "catalogComments": "", "catalogPrereqCoreq": "Prerequisite: grade of B+ or higher in KOREA 2210\u00a0or KOREA 3302, or online placement test (collt.lrc.cornell.edu/).", "catalogPrereq": null, "catalogCoreq": null, "catalogFee": "", "catalogSatisfiesReq": "", "catalogPermission": "", "catalogCourseSubfield": "", "catalogOutcomes": null, "acadCareer": "UG", "acadGroup": "AS", "lastTermsOffered": null, "exploreCriteriaIds": []}]}, "message": null, "meta": {"copyright": "Cornell University, Office of the University Registrar", "rosterDttm": "2023-04-13T14:00:07-0400", "catalogDttm": "2023-04-12T19:14:04-0400"}}